WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:03.239
Chris Hemsworth is one of those rare actors
who can do it all.

00:00:03.239 --> 00:00:07.420
The Australian star clearly excels in action
films, considering he's the mighty Thor of

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:09.639
the Avengers in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:09.639 --> 00:00:12.980
But he can also handle fantasy, comedy, drama,
and even horror.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.850
This kind of versatility means that Hemsworth
is regularly on set, and all those long hours

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.020
can make even the biggest movie stars a little
loopy.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.250
Well, the results have been caught on film.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:24.560
Here are some of the best Chris Hemsworth
bloopers.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.560
Juggling act

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.830
Mjolnir, Thor's mighty hammer, is unmovable
by pretty much everyone except the God of

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:31.010
Thunder himself.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.950
It's probably the most famous object in Norse
mythology, and certainly the most famous tool

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:38.850
in comics this side of Captain America's shield
or Batman's utility belt.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:43.050
Of course, the hammer Hemsworth carries around
in all the Marvel films is just a lightweight

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.050
prop.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.300
And apparently, he can toss it around and
juggle it quite easily.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.320
Okay, maybe not easily.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:58.680
Joke-busters

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.239
Before the cameras roll, actors carefully
memorize their lines.

00:01:02.239 --> 00:01:04.720
Preparation is important for a good performance,
of course.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.830
But familiarization with the material is critical
in comedies — if actors don't know what's

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.940
coming, they're liable to laugh and ruin takes.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.490
Now imagine how tricky it gets once everyone
is improvising on the spot.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:19.070
Take the 2016 Ghostbusters, for example, when
Hemsworth had to describe why he likes hot

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:20.070
dogs:

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:22.940
"It contains all two food groups…"

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:28.380
"Dogs and buns… (laughs) sorry."

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:31.750
Director Paul Feig encourages
actors to try out ideas that pop into their

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.590
heads during filming, and even throws out
suggestions himself.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:38.240
But sometimes, when a joke is brand new, it's
hard to deliver it with a straight face.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:39.700
"I slept through a fire once.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.140
Didn't even smell it."

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.040
"It was in your house?"

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:43.660
"Yeah."

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:46.030
"The whole house burned down around me."

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:47.720
"Yeah, f---!"

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:52.530
And once a bad case of the giggles has set
in, there may be no coming back from it.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.060
"The fire was in your house?"

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.060
"Yeah.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:57.260
And the whole house went down.

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:02.500
F---, it upsets me now! (laughs)"

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:03.500
Just say it

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:07.600
Certain scenes in Thor: The Dark World between
Hemsworth and Natalie Portman's character,

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:10.369
Jane Foster, are tender and emotionally powerful.

00:02:10.369 --> 00:02:13.239
Well...they were supposed to be.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:16.080
"But I do know this…"

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:16.580
"Know what?"

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.620
"I know…"

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:19.220
"That what?"

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.719
Come on, Thor, just tell her how you feel.

00:02:24.719 --> 00:02:29.580
"Jane, I don't know what happened or where
you were…"

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:30.930
Huntsman holdups

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:34.920
Hemsworth plays the the title role in the
Huntsman films, the action-packed adaptations

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:38.739
of the Snow White folktale, collected and
popularized by the Brothers Grimm in 19th

00:02:38.739 --> 00:02:39.739
century Germany.

00:02:39.739 --> 00:02:43.549
The films actually take place long before
that — they have a strong Medieval, fairy

00:02:43.549 --> 00:02:44.549
tale vibe.

00:02:44.549 --> 00:02:47.129
At any rate, it's long before the dawn of
mechanical flight.

00:02:47.129 --> 00:02:50.969
Which means Hemsworth had to put the acting
on pause whenever filming was interrupted

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.220
by scene-stealing airplanes.

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:03.680
But planes weren't the only things that held
up production.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.580
Unfortunately, there was one on-set diva who
wanted nothing to do with poor Hemsworth.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:21.269
And then there were those moments where he
had no one to blame but himself.

00:03:21.269 --> 00:03:26.310
"Hang on… the worst-paced acting ever."

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:27.469
Do a little dance

00:03:27.469 --> 00:03:31.519
What if you witnessed one of the strongest
and most unbreakable objects on the planet

00:03:31.519 --> 00:03:35.760
crack in half and reveal itself for what it
truly is — some flimsy little objects glued

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:36.760
together?

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:38.800
Let's just say, a little dancing solves most
problems.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:48.340
Cape gone wild

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:52.329
The three most defining characteristics of
Thor are the powerful hammer in his hand,

00:03:52.329 --> 00:03:55.920
that long blond hair, and his red cape that
ripples in the wind behind him.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.560
Well, two out of three ain't bad.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:01.809
Because on the set of this standalone Thor
film, Hemsworth's most temperamental co-star

00:04:01.809 --> 00:04:02.900
was… that cape.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:15.059
In addition to the cape issues on the Dark
World set, it apparently wasn't clear to some

00:04:15.059 --> 00:04:17.900
people whether certain scenes had finished
filming or not...

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.840
"I believe you were and you weren't."

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:23.680
"What the hell's this?

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:26.080
We're still going!"

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:28.240
Thanks for watching!

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:30.669
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:33.000
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

